**Figure 1.** Light curve of the 30,000,000 photon arrival times in `photons.f32` from release `photons-v1` of paper-repo (downloaded file SHA-256 `af343d7a…2edae`, matching `photons.sha256`), in 1200 one-second bins (black step line; photons per 1 s bin, numerically photons s⁻¹). The red curve is the Poisson maximum-likelihood fit of a constant background plus a Gaussian burst, integrated over each bin; the dashed line is the fitted background rate (20,003.1 photons s⁻¹). Lower panel: Pearson residuals (n − m)/√m with ±2 guides; Pearson χ² = 1214.6 for 1196 degrees of freedom. Fit values and 95% profile-likelihood intervals are in the fit table (from experiment-repo `results/fit.json`).
